codex
The Windows capture path now creates the owned browser before entering `timeout`, and its operation is finalized explicitly afterward. Windows console signals are being passed into that orchestration as cancellation, so they cancel the inner work and still await cleanup; the Unix signal branch remains on its existing path. I’m adding deterministic finalization tests and replacing the Windows test’s sleep-based readiness check with a reported process tree and bounded assertions.
