While reviewing the native test’s post-teardown assertions, I caught an important Windows detail: reopening an already exited descendant by PID can fail because the OS may have discarded its process object. I’m tightening the test to open and retain synchronization handles for both reported helper processes before teardown, then wait on those handles afterward. That makes the termination assertions reliable and tied to the exact fixture processes.
